utomation across the entire agreement lifecycle; and provides e-signature solution that enables sending and signing of agreements on various devices; Contract Lifecycle Management (CLM), which automates workflows across the entire agreement process; and Document Generation streamlines the process of generating new, custom agreements. It also provides Identify, a signer-identification option for checking government-issued IDs; Standards-Based Signatures, which support signatures that involve digital certificates; Monitor that uses advanced analytics; Notary which enables notaries public to conduct remote online notarization transactions; and Web Forms. In addition, the company offers Real Estate for eSignature that provides a way for brokers and agents to manage the entire real estate transaction digitally. eSignature and CLM are Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program (FedRAMP), an authorized version of DocuSign eSignature for U.S. federal government agencies; and life sciences modules that support compliance with the electronic signature practices. The company sells its products through direct and partner-assisted sales, and digital self-service purchasing. DocuSign, Inc. was incorporated in 2003 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Allan C. Thygesen | President, CEO & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $457K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 24%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $150K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $88K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["DocuSign, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $15.1B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +10.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 12% cost of capital \u2014 a 8-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 78% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $1.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 33 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.77\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 19% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 58% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 3 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5795991454563996},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $10.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Trending Stock Docusign Inc. (DOCU) a Buy Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028496/is-trending-stock-docusign-inc-docu-a-buy-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cmost_searched_stocks-3028496","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794488403.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here's Why DocuSign (DOCU) is a Strong Growth Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028122/here-s-why-docusign-docu-is-a-strong-growth-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_growth_score-3028122","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794428226.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.71,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Docusign (DOCU) & Its Competitors Critical Comparison","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/docusign-docu-its-competitors-critical-comparison.html","da